#: src/macros/intro/how.md:6
msgid "How Do Macros Work"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/how.md:8
msgid ""
"To understand how macros work, it helps to look at the pipeline of how a "
"compiler processes your code:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/how.md:11
msgid ""
"**Source Code:** The raw text files written by the programmer, consisting of "
"a sequence of characters in some character set (in Rust, Unicode characters "
"in UTF-8)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/how.md:14
msgid ""
"**Lexical Analysis (Lexing):** The compiler delimits the raw text into a "
"sequence of **tokens** (e.g., `fn`, `main`, identifiers, punctuation, "
"literals)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/how.md:17
msgid ""
"**Syntactic Analysis (Parsing):** Based on the language's grammar, the "
"compiler organizes the sequence of tokens into an **Abstract Syntax Tree "
"(AST)** that captures the hierarchical structure of the program."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/how.md:21
msgid "Source Code"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/how.md:21
msgid "Tokenized Rust (Approx.)"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/how.md:21
msgid "AST Rust (Approx.)"
msgstr ""

