msgid "`fn main() {}`"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/how.md:23
msgid "`Ident: fn`, `Ident: main`, `Group: ()`, `Group: {}`"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/how.md:23
msgid "`Fn: ident=main, block=...`"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/how.md:25
msgid ""
"Different macro systems hook into different parts of this pipeline, offering "
"different tradeoffs between expressiveness and safety."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/how.md:28
msgid ""
"We'll look at the macro system used in C and C++ via the C Preprocessor, "
"which is well-known, and contrast this with Rust's macro system."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/how.md:34
msgid ""
"Explain that the AST is a structured tree that represents what the program "
"actually means semantically."
msgstr ""
